      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e615ecf5_c4b15ea8",
        "filename": "ui/terminal/format.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 114,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074628
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-11T23:25:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This would be closer to the \"all\" filter in Bazel, where my understanding is that package/subpackages is more commonly used (but we don\u0027t really have the same concept in most builds).\n\nThe direction we\u0027d like to be heading long term is to actually fix up the code so that there just aren\u0027t warnings printed by the compilers and other tools. We\u0027ve gotten fairly close in the past with a few targets, but never quite gotten the point where we can make it a requirement. http://go/android-silent-build was one of the docs, but it really comes down to -Werror/-Wno-..., filtering output, removing debug prints by default, etc.",
      "parentUuid": "c1f87e21_5e16b969",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 114,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 114,
        "endChar": 7
      },
      "revId": "512cf80d880cf592a88013a395ab14f65a6cc5d4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "93c2fd4e_da3502bb",
        "filename": "ui/terminal/format.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 114,
      "author": {
        "id": 1067098
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-11T23:47:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think that every project with build warning spam has a long term goal of cleaning it up. Unfortunately little progress is ever made due to diffusion of responsibility. You will observe that that doc is from 2017 and references bugs from 2015, and the situation is still the same. I doubt that the situation will improve especially if the project is unstaffed. In the meantime, all developers will have to put up with spammy builds.\n\nOn the other hand, if we accept warning spam as a reality, we have this simple CL that fixes the spam entirely for those who choose to opt into it.",
      "parentUuid": "e615ecf5_c4b15ea8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 114,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 114,
        "endChar": 7
      },
